.IX Title "EVP_MD-ML-DSA-MU 7ossl"
.TH EVP_MD-ML-DSA-MU 7ossl "2026-04-14" "4.0.0" "OpenSSL"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
EVP_MD\-ML\-DSA\-MU \- The ML\-DSA\-MU EVP_MD implementation
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Support for computing the value of external mu for ML-DSA using the \fB\s-1EVP_MD\s0\fR \s-1API.\s0
.PP
Normally the value of \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR is calculated internally as part of an ML-DSA
sign or verify operation. \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR is defined as:
    mu = \s-1SHAKE256\s0(tr || M', 64)
.PP
Where \fBtr\fR is the hash of the encoded public key, and, for Pure (ML-DSA):
    M' = 0x00 || ctx_len || ctx || message
.PP
In cases where prehashing the message is required, \s-1FIPS 204\s0 allows
the \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR calculation to be done externally and then \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR can be passed to
ML-DSA sign or verify operations.
.PP
PreHash (HASH-ML-DSA) is also supported and uses:
    M' = 0x01 || ctx_len || ctx || \s-1OID\s0 || HashedMessage
.PP
The output \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR value can then be supplied as an input to \s-1\fIEVP_SIGNATURE\-ML\-DSA\s0\fR\|(7)
using the ML-DSA Signature Parameter \fB\s-1OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_MU\s0\fR (i.e. \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR).
This allows larger messages to be hashed (or hidden) before they are passed to
pure ML-DSA sign or verify operations.
.SS "Identities"
.IX Subsection "Identities"
This implementation is available with the \s-1FIPS\s0 provider as well as the
default provider, and is identified with the name \*(L"ML-DSA-MU\*(R".
.SS "Parameters"
.IX Subsection "Parameters"
This implementation supports the following settable \s-1\fIOSSL_PARAM\s0\fR\|(3) parameters:
.ie n .IP """pub"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PUB_KEY\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.el .IP "``pub'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PUB_KEY\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item "pub (OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PUB_KEY) <octet string>"
A \fBML-DSA\fR encoded public key value of size 1312, 1952 or 2592 bytes
depending on the respective key type of \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-44\s0\fR, \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-65\s0\fR or \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-87\s0\fR.
This can be retrieved from a \s-1\fIEVP_PKEY\-ML\-DSA\s0\fR\|(7) key by calling
EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(key, \s-1OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY,\s0 pub, sizeof(pub), &publen)
This parameter \s-1MUST\s0 be set or an error will occur.
.ie n .IP """context-string"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_CONTEXT_STRING\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.el .IP "``context-string'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_CONTEXT_STRING\s0\fR) <octet string>" 4
.IX Item "context-string (OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_CONTEXT_STRING) <octet string>"
An optional string of octets with length at most 255. By default it is the empty string.
.ie n .IP """digest"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_DIGEST\s0\fR) <utf8 string>" 4
.el .IP "``digest'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_DIGEST\s0\fR) <utf8 string>" 4
.IX Item "digest (OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_DIGEST) <utf8 string>"
An optional parameter related to \*(L"HASH-ML-DSA\*(R". If used it determines the \s-1OID\s0 in
the definition of PreHash M' above.
.Sp
When this parameter is not specified, pure ML-DSA \f(CW\*(C`mu\*(C'\fR is computed, and the
input data is expected to be the full message, otherwise the input data must
be the result of prehashing the message with the corresponding digest algorithm.
.Sp
The HASH-ML-DSA variant is available to enable specialised use-cases,
in which signing the full message with pure ML-DSA is not practical, and
the external-mu \s-1API\s0 is a viable alternative.
HASH-ML-DSA is not used in protocols such as X509 & \s-1CMS \s0(See \s-1RFC 9981\s0 and 9982),
and is not presently implemented as an independent OpenSSL signature algorithm.
.Sp
It is the users responsibility to chose a digest that has the minimum required
security strength. To match the security category for \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-44\s0\fR, \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-65\s0\fR
and \fB\s-1ML\-DSA\-87\s0\fR the user should chose a digest that has a security strength of
at least 128 bits, 192 bits and 256 bits respectively.
.Sp
OpenSSL accepts the following digest names:
.RS 4
.ie n .IP """\s-1SHA\-224""\s0 and ""\s-1SHA3\-224""\s0" 4
.el .IP "``\s-1SHA\-224''\s0 and ``\s-1SHA3\-224''\s0" 4
.IX Item "SHA-224 and SHA3-224"
These digests have a security strength of 112 bits.
.ie n .IP """\s-1SHA\-256""\s0 and ""\s-1SHA3\-256""\s0" 4
.el .IP "``\s-1SHA\-256''\s0 and ``\s-1SHA3\-256''\s0" 4
.IX Item "SHA-256 and SHA3-256"
These digests have a security strength of 128 bits.
.ie n .IP """\s-1SHA\-384""\s0 and ""\s-1SHA3\-384""\s0" 4
.el .IP "``\s-1SHA\-384''\s0 and ``\s-1SHA3\-384''\s0" 4
.IX Item "SHA-384 and SHA3-384"
These digests have a security strength of 192 bits.
.ie n .IP """\s-1SHA\-512""\s0 and ""\s-1SHA3\-512""\s0" 4
.el .IP "``\s-1SHA\-512''\s0 and ``\s-1SHA3\-512''\s0" 4
.IX Item "SHA-512 and SHA3-512"
These digests have a security strength of 256 bits.
.ie n .IP """\s-1SHAKE\-128""\s0 and ""\s-1SHAKE\-256""\s0" 4
.el .IP "``\s-1SHAKE\-128''\s0 and ``\s-1SHAKE\-256''\s0" 4
.IX Item "SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256"
For \s-1SHAKE\-128\s0 and \s-1SHAKE\-256\s0 the expected \s-1XOF\s0 digest
lengths are 32 and 64 respectively which correspond to a security strength of
128 and 256 bits respectively.
.RE
.RS 4
.Sp
The total size of the \f(CW\*(C`HashedMessage\*(C'\fR passed to \fIEVP_DigestUpdate()\fR \s-1MUST\s0 match
the size of the digest.
.RE
.ie n .IP """properties"" (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PROPERTIES\s0\fR) <utf8 string>" 4
.el .IP "``properties'' (\fB\s-1OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PROPERTIES\s0\fR) <utf8 string>" 4
.IX Item "properties (OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PROPERTIES) <utf8 string>"
Sets the properties to be queried when trying to fetch the underlying digest.
.SS "Gettable Parameters"
.IX Subsection "Gettable Parameters"
This implementation supports the common gettable parameters described
in \fIEVP_MD\-common\fR\|(7).
.SH "CONFORMING TO"
.IX Header "CONFORMING TO"
\&\s-1FIPS 204\s0 and
https://csrc.nist.gov/csrc/media/Projects/post\-quantum\-cryptography/documents/faq/fips204\-sec6\-03192025.pdf
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
To generate external 'mu' given an existing ML-DSA key and a large message:
.PP
.Vb 6
\&    calculate_mu(EVP_PKEY *pkey, const unsigned char *msg, size_t msglen,
\&                 const unsigned char *ctx, size_t ctxlen, unsigned char mu[64])
\&    {
\&        unsigned char pub[2592];
\&        size_t publen = 0, chunk;
\&        OSSL_PARAM params[4], *p = params;
\&
\&        /* Retrieve the ML\-DSA encoded public key */
\&        EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY,
\&                                        pub, sizeof(pub), &publen);
\&
\&        *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_PUB_KEY, pub, publen);
\&        /* This is an optional parameter */
\&        if (ctx != NULL && ctxlen != 0)
\&            *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_CONTEXT_STRING, ctx, ctxlen);
\&        /*
\&         * Optionally we could also set the digest name for HASH\-ML\-DSA
\&         * *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_MU_DIGEST, "SHA\-512", 0);
\&         */
\&        *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
\&
\&        mdctx = EVP_MD_CTX_new();
\&        md = EVP_MD_fetch(libctx, "ML\-DSA\-MU", NULL);
\&        EVP_DigestInit_ex2(mdctx, md, params);
\&        /* Call EVP_DigestUpdate() multiple times to stream the message */
\&        while (msglen != 0) {
\&            /* Account for the last chunk being less than 64 */
\&            chunk = (msglen >= 64) ? 64 : msglen;
\&            EVP_DigestUpdate(mdctx, msg, chunk);
\&            msg += chunk;
\&            msglen \-= chunk;
\&        }
\&        EVP_DigestFinalXOF(mdctx, mu, sizeof(mu))
\&    }
.Ve
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\s-1\fIEVP_SIGNATURE\-ML\-DSA\s0\fR\|(7),
\&\s-1\fIEVP_PKEY\-ML\-DSA\s0\fR\|(7),
\&\fIprovider\-digest\fR\|(7),
\&\s-1\fIOSSL_PROVIDER\-FIPS\s0\fR\|(7),
\&\fIOSSL_PROVIDER\-default\fR\|(7)
.SH "HISTORY"
.IX Header "HISTORY"
The \fBML-DSA-MU\fR pseudo-digest was added in OpenSSL 4.0.0.
